#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447159 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172089 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "973cf948-eeb3-5c46-b0ac-ee0307a8043a" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing Line Integrals of Unity Over Polar Curves"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0081acc5-b8a0-5432-9f86-16b58fe1f445" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{8+10\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta +10\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447091} {:answer/id #uuid "1015c73e-191b-5d23-bc1d-08512f03b481" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+6{sin}^{2}⁡3\\theta +8\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447093} {:answer/id #uuid "369565c3-561a-50ca-9be4-d934f4abc68d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta +6\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447100} {:answer/id #uuid "609847c3-196c-5c58-9386-82fb40230109" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{10+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta +8{cos}^{2}⁡3\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447111} {:answer/id #uuid "8a907a7b-6b1a-50eb-9d99-ac2cfde55650" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{10\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta +9{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447117}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "609847c3-196c-5c58-9386-82fb40230109" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{10+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta +8{cos}^{2}⁡3\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447111} :answer-field/id #uuid "970ad32f-3bc8-5eae-a83f-06f38e693fb2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447146}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8c80223d-79b2-5d97-8d88-3fa6275a012a" :question/math-academy-id "q-123377" :question/problem "![](images/3b/3b8ef36c29d1babc5c3ccf1d474678a18ed5937b883e026d18d5c7ea1aaaa3f5.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r=3+\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta \\,$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi ,$ shown above?" :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\text{d}s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\\theta )$ for ${\\theta }_{1}\\le \\theta \\le {\\theta }_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=3+\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expression for our line integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{(3+\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta )^{2}+(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta )^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{9+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡3\\theta +9{cos}^{2}⁡3\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{9+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta +1+8{cos}^{2}⁡3\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{10+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta +8{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405029 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172089 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "973cf948-eeb3-5c46-b0ac-ee0307a8043a" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing Line Integrals of Unity Over Polar Curves"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ac3d5894-f4c5-5d9e-ab7c-cd4cec7b9228" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{3+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta }\\,\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405031} {:answer/id #uuid "098ef428-487b-52de-8bb3-157513d5af5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{5+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta }\\,\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405032} {:answer/id #uuid "7ec24e38-78a7-59a2-bcbd-116c50a31d93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta }\\,\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405033} {:answer/id #uuid "2fff1e42-09de-569f-8b26-6742481f41f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{5-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta }\\,\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405034} {:answer/id #uuid "a5a7a56e-be07-55b4-a841-3621b9f27de7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{5-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta }\\,\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405035}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2fff1e42-09de-569f-8b26-6742481f41f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{5-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta }\\,\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405034} :answer-field/id #uuid "5aaf3974-45a7-5d36-b332-ebb301287f47" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186405030}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9debd71f-7b2d-5a32-ae10-ca946736e9d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-123458" :question/problem "Which of the following gives ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s$ with the arc-length integrand simplified pointwise in the given polar angle $\\theta$ (on each smooth piece, without reparametrizing), where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r=\\sqrt{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta }\\,$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi $ ?" :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\text{d}s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\\theta )$ for ${\\theta }_{1}\\le \\theta \\le {\\theta }_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nWhere $1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta>0$, $r=\\sqrt{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta }\\,$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta }{\\sqrt{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta }}.\n$$\n\nApplying the arc-length formula piecewise between the finitely many zeros of $r$, the expression for our line integral is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{(\\sqrt{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta })^{2}+{(\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta }{\\sqrt{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta }})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta )+\\frac{4{cos}^{2}⁡4\\theta }{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{\\frac{(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta )^{2}+4(1-{sin}^{2}⁡4\\theta )}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{\\frac{(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta )^{2}+4(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta )(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta )}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{\\frac{(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta )[1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta +4-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta ]}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{5-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta }\\,\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483421 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172089 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "973cf948-eeb3-5c46-b0ac-ee0307a8043a" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing Line Integrals of Unity Over Polar Curves"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "236acfde-42f2-51a3-82ca-3600a09ce0a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482876} {:answer/id #uuid "38ff41e9-dd02-5d21-92a8-581369d18b20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +1}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482910} {:answer/id #uuid "8eac4e6e-fe81-5a84-9636-cabf10c5314f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483061} {:answer/id #uuid "acc1c101-f384-5d1e-ab31-e736b726cbf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +1}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483104} {:answer/id #uuid "b1c5c96c-0c63-5cb2-88af-e9d02ac33333" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483115}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8eac4e6e-fe81-5a84-9636-cabf10c5314f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483061} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf074d1f-8612-5220-b189-30860f156e17" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483319}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e4160743-42ed-5b1d-80ee-6f99ed405134" :question/math-academy-id "q-149786" :question/problem "![](images/24/24f7ae31455abc10e60814b6b599966c92680422432c82f6cc7386d6d414f29c.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +1$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi ,$ shown above?" :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\text{d}s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\\theta )$ for ${\\theta }_{1}\\le \\theta \\le {\\theta }_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expression for our line integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +1)}^{2}+{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +1+{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +1+1}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363363 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172089 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "973cf948-eeb3-5c46-b0ac-ee0307a8043a" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing Line Integrals of Unity Over Polar Curves"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ec25039-c0fd-56ca-b984-bd9349c79ceb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{e}^{-\\theta /2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363365} {:answer/id #uuid "93316eec-08b8-5888-a518-1f7f028efff6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{e}^{-\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363366} {:answer/id #uuid "ddd3e2e0-b449-5ae9-bfe5-39ae00b8ab32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{e}^{-2\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363367} {:answer/id #uuid "827145a1-4259-51ff-8504-aef48c2e2ead" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{e}^{-2\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363368} {:answer/id #uuid "0a472974-80e2-5c15-a84b-22f9c2f5a79c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{e}^{-\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363369}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93316eec-08b8-5888-a518-1f7f028efff6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{e}^{-\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363366} :answer-field/id #uuid "5703c778-a247-5102-af88-f5464e7312d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363364}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "929c6f43-55a6-50e3-98c8-0627bab8c6ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-149788" :question/problem "![](images/03/03cacb8c2da76ff806a3f8a41cf18d3b57f67eeb60d6efa0cdfbfce770496c60.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r={e}^{-\\theta }\\,$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},$ shown above?" :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\text{d}s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\\theta )$ for ${\\theta }_{1}\\le \\theta \\le {\\theta }_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r={e}^{-\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=-{e}^{-\\theta }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expression for our line integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{({e}^{-\\theta })}^{2}+{(-{e}^{\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{e}^{-2\\theta }+{e}^{-2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{2{e}^{-2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{e}^{-\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363370 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172089 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "973cf948-eeb3-5c46-b0ac-ee0307a8043a" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing Line Integrals of Unity Over Polar Curves"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94106bf7-442c-57b7-a8d4-7d3725cd3301" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}\\sqrt{1+15{sin}^{2}⁡4\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363372} {:answer/id #uuid "a0f17b3f-b619-5663-a742-8cd16caad422" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}\\sqrt{1+64{sin}^{2}⁡4\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363373} {:answer/id #uuid "2f268941-c5e1-5f87-9aff-31416118fe66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}\\sqrt{1+8{sin}^{2}⁡4\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363374} {:answer/id #uuid "63cf36ad-cc0f-5781-9b02-c40c452e845e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}\\sqrt{1+12{sin}^{2}⁡2\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363375} {:answer/id #uuid "eac417bd-f5e6-53b0-85c1-fea6d7f50ec2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}\\sqrt{1+40{sin}^{2}⁡2\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363376}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94106bf7-442c-57b7-a8d4-7d3725cd3301" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}\\sqrt{1+15{sin}^{2}⁡4\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363372} :answer-field/id #uuid "388c2572-dc24-57d0-9cb1-bc6bf8263984" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363371}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cd418bfc-f7c5-506e-bc72-5623879aa6a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-149798" :question/problem "![](images/c6/c6556825089b3b475615ed4a8ebf9eff2e6db3d76eb26103312f736a3e114793.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta $ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{8},$ shown above?" :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\text{d}s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\\theta )$ for ${\\theta }_{1}\\le \\theta \\le {\\theta }_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expression for our line integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}\\sqrt{{(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta )}^{2}+{(-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}\\sqrt{4{cos}^{2}⁡4\\theta +64{sin}^{2}⁡4\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}\\sqrt{4{cos}^{2}⁡4\\theta +4{sin}^{2}⁡4\\theta +60{sin}^{2}⁡4\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}\\sqrt{4+60{sin}^{2}⁡4\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}\\sqrt{1+15{sin}^{2}⁡4\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
